==Trivia==
*The name Naala (ナーラ ''Nāra'') may be a reference to the Japanese city of [[wikipedia:Nara (city)|Nara]], which is famous for its deer. In fact, Naala and Nara sound almost the same in Japanese.
*Ultima Beast Naala appears to be based on the [[wikipedia:Qilin|qilin/kirin]], a holy, unicorn-like beast from Chinese mythology that is often depicted with deer-like traits, particularly in Japan. [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Elder Beast Naala]]'s Japanese description refers to it as a ''[[wikipedia:Raijū|raijū]]'' (雷獣, "thunder-beast"), a Japanese legendary creature that has a body made of lightning and is represented with the form of many different animals, including a deer or kirin.
**Naala may specifically be based on [[wikia:monsterhunter:Kirin|Kirin]] from ''Monster Hunter'', as its ability to rapidly call down series of lightning bolts is very similar to ''Monster Hunter''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s Kirin's attacks and [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoths]] tend to be references to ''Monster Hunter''.
*Ultima Beast Naala may represent [[wikipedia:Eikþyrnir|Eikþyrnir]], a heavenly stag in Norse mythology. Awakened Naala is stated to be holy, and Eikþyrnir eats from [[wikipedia:Læraðr|Læraðr]], a tree often identified with [[wikipedia:Yggdrasil|Yggdrasil]]—a possible inspiration for the [[Media:Bg1028.gif|huge, glowing tree]] in the last four [[Uncanny Legends]] stages. The dew that drips from Eikþyrnir's glowing antlers flows into [[wikipedia:Hvergelmir|Hvergelmir]], one of the wellsprings at Yggdrasil's roots, creating rivers that sustain life; this may be referenced by the stage before [[Immortal Zenith]], [[Silver Current]], whose Japanese name confirms that it refers to a water current. Eikþyrnir stands upon one of the afterlife locations, [[wikipedia:Valhalla|Valhalla]], which may correlate or contrast with [[Immortal Zenith]], whose Japanese name (天寿を授ける頂 ''Tenju o Sazukeru Itadaki'') can be literally translated as "The Summit That Bestows Natural Lifespans".
*The Japanese descriptions of [[Ganglion (Uber Rare Cat)|Ganglion]], whose enemy counterpart [[Ensanglion the Calamity|Ensanglion]] is a Behemoth, and Ultima Beast Naala, another powerful, ancient Behemoth, both use the word 始祖 ''shiso'' (founder or originator; the first person to start something, or the first in a lineage). Ganglion is said to be the founder/originator of all dragons (全てのドラゴンの始祖 ''subete no doragon no shiso''), while Naala is revered as the founder/originator of all beasts (全ての獣の始祖 ''subete no kemono no shiso'').
*Ultima Beast Naala and Elder Beast Naala are the first characters to have multi-hit attacks with different effective ranges on each hit.
*Along with [[Ragin' Gory]] and [[Wild Doge]], Ultima Beast Naala was one of the three enemies that were updated to have the Behemoth type in [[Version 11.5 Update|Version 11.5]].
*Ultima Beast Naala and [[Ancient Magamojoe]] are the only Behemoths to share the same title in their Japanese names. Both are titled Chō Kojū (超古獣, "Super Ancient Beast").
*Ultima Beast Naala's icon shows all of the lightning from its feet at once, which doesn't happen in-game.

